# Rebuild "Bismillah Motors" as a cPanel-Deployable Full-Stack App (React + PHP/MySQL)

## Project context

You are regenerating an existing e-commerce site called **Bismillah Motors** (a motorcycle parts & stickers store in Jashore, Bangladesh). The current version is deployed at https://bismillah-full.onrender.com and uses React + Vite + Tailwind on the frontend and Node.js/Express on the backend.

**The problem:** The current backend requires Node.js, which most cheap shared cPanel hosting plans do NOT support. The static-only zip that was previously produced is missing the backend entirely, so order placement, admin login, and order tracking all fail on cPanel.

**Your task:** Rebuild the app so the frontend stays React/Vite, but the backend becomes **pure PHP 8 + MySQL/MariaDB**. The final deliverable is a downloadable ZIP produced by a GitHub Actions workflow, structured so the user can extract it directly into cPanel's `public_html/` folder and have everything work end-to-end after importing a SQL schema and editing one config file.

---

## Target deployment environment

- **Hosting:** Standard shared cPanel hosting (Hostinger, Namecheap, Bluehost, A2, etc.)
- **Server stack:** Apache + PHP 7.4 or 8.x + MySQL/MariaDB
- **No Node.js available on the server** (only used during the GitHub Actions build)
- **No Composer available** — PHP must be written by hand using only built-in extensions (PDO, json, hash, openssl)
- **Single domain, single origin** — frontend and API both served from `public_html/`

